{"id":"death-eternal","name":"Death, Eternal","aliases":["Death"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:death-eternal"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Death","text":"May be simply defined as the termination of life. It is represented under a variety of aspects in Scripture: (1.) “The dust shall return to the earth as it was” (Eccl. 12:7). (2.) “Thou takest away their breath, they die” (Ps. 104:29). (3.) It is the dissolution of “our earthly house of this tabernacle” (2 Cor. 5:1); the “putting off this tabernacle” (2 Pet. 1:13, 14). (4.) Being “unclothed” (2 Cor. 5:3, 4). (5.) “Falling on sleep” (Ps. 76:5; Jer. 51:39; Acts 13:36; 2 Pet. 3:9. (6.) “I go whence I shall not return” (Job 10:21); “Make me to know mine end” (Ps. 39:4); “to depart” (Phil. 1:23). The grave is represented as “the gates of death” (Job 38:17; Ps. 9:13; 107:18). The gloomy silence of the grave is spoken of under the figure of the “shadow of death” (Jer. 2:6). Death is the effect of sin (Heb. 2:14), and not a “debt of nature.” It is but once (9:27), universal (Gen. 3:19), …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G2288","lemma":"θάνατος","xlit":"thánatos","gloss":"death","kjv":"X deadly, death","count":10,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G166","lemma":"αἰώνιος","xlit":"aiṓnios","gloss":"perpetual","kjv":"eternal, for ever, everlasting, world","count":5,"share":0.13},{"strong":"G4442","lemma":"πῦρ","xlit":"pŷr","gloss":"\"fire\"","kjv":"fiery, fire","count":5,"share":0.13},{"strong":"G2222","lemma":"ζωή","xlit":"zōḗ","gloss":"life","kjv":"life","count":5,"share":0.13},{"strong":"G2976","lemma":"Λάζαρος","xlit":"Lázaros","gloss":"Lazarus , the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Lazarus","count":3,"share":0.07},{"strong":"G266","lemma":"ἁμαρτία","xlit":"hamartía","gloss":"a sin","kjv":"offence, sin","count":4,"share":0.1}],"verses":["John.8.51","Rom.1.32","Rom.6.16","Rom.6.21","Rom.6.23","Jas.1.15","Jas.5.20","Rev.2.11","Rev.20.6","Rev.21.8","Ps.9.17","Prov.14.12","Dan.12.2","Matt.7.13","Matt.10.2